    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d447">

                <pb facs="0711" n="683" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v03/pg683"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340/7–553: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The United States Delegation to the
                            Economic and Social Council to the Department
                            of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1953-07-05T11:00:00+01:00">July 5, 1953—11
                            a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    Ecosoc 12. In light Ecosoc 4 and supplement<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d447-f1"/> likely Chinese representation issue raised on report
                    credentials. In unlikely case issue raised inform 1(B) Socec 1 USDel intends handle issue in accordance <pb
                        facs="0712" n="684" xml:id="pg684"/> position paper moving adjournment
                    debate for duration sixteenth session stating effect would not only be (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">a</hi>) continued seating of Chinese Nationalist
                    representatives but also (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) rejection request for
                    inclusion item on agenda. UK agrees.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ward</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
